  "notes": ["Descriptive statistics summarize 217 matched individuals (104 core and 113 peripheral) in each reference arm. SD is the sample standard deviation among individuals, not among independent populations.", "Class means weight individuals equally; no population-level independent-replicate test is implied.", "Depth and breadth denominators refer to each complete assembly or its observed covered bases; they are not matched homologous RAD regions and are not genotype missingness.", "The two reference arms use the same cleaned reads. Existing A. nanus PCA scores were reused; new A. mongolicus variants were called with bcftools, not the historical two-caller intersection.", "No new inferential tests, PCA alignment, Procrustes analysis, functional-load or genomic-offset reruns were performed by this reporting script.", "PCA agreement must be assessed separately from the plotted point distributions; these summaries do not automatically establish robustness.", "Fractions are stored unrounded (0-1); multiply by 100 for percentages. Paired differences of fractions become percentage points when multiplied by 100."],
